F_0001": "\\ref{quot-lemma-complexes-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{quot-lemma-complexes-open-neg-exts-vanishing}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{quot-proposition-isom}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30b3d8942ce4fd2dc06f67d1eb0ace1355259b053f0be0bae9a76dc029f02488", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:afa440bf80d310f516b5c7e1145450321f189d3c20858706a2db54c2573395c9", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThe representability of the diagonal by algebraic spaces\nwas shown in Quot, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFrom the proof we find that we have to show:\ngiven a scheme <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> and objects\n<MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are objects of the fibre category\nof <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008>\nis affine and of finite presentation.\nHere <MATH_0009> is the functor\n<MATH_0010>\nwhere <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> are the derived pullbacks of <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>\nto <MATH_0015>. Consider the functor <MATH_0016> defined\nby the rule\n<MATH_0017>\nBy Quot, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthis is an algebraic space affine and of finite presentation over <MATH_0018>.\nThe same is true for <MATH_0019>, <MATH_0020>, and\n<MATH_0021>. Therefore we see that\n<MATH_0022>\nwhere <MATH_0023>\nand <MATH_0024> (compare with the proof of\nQuot, Proposition <REF_0003>). Thus\n<MATH_0025> is affine over <MATH_0026> as a fibre product of\nschemes affine over <MATH_0027>. Similarly, <MATH_0028> is\nof finite presentation over <MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:652fda69c4a8e1ad5c9c867eac76e821ad89e8f3237a6729681b97606dce1c08", "unit_id": "inventory:moduli:0DPW:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:fd764b4c65556c40c6355a24f3c603806dfc9860c96df568557563e3f4f4ed3f", "hash": "sha256:fd764b4c65556c40c6355a24f3c603806dfc9860c9